{"title":"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6(like_solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6(like solution 2)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7(A_simpler_version_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7(A simpler version of Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Sam Vandervelde</i>) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a>.  Define a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bf6d7656718f44b05db794584495187f058493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" /> and, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ff8ea020546fb6e8c90abbfb0b50802eee802d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be the unique integer in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ea63a560468c8663c284ac35eddc72cf5fbb98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_k \\le k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5a1c5ce08278939dc6a5f9348a453ed5e94680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisible\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Divisible\">divisible</a> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  For instance, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18fb781bb0840e30c7a894eac0d3a0f67fcd3157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> the obtained sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d8c5e11f1f6a2adbc48812087abd72527f8f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9, 1, 2, 0, 3, 3, 3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a82e7c7dbf7b035a66b5890ec80463b4c3e8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> eventually becomes <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constant</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bdc4c41a6437428498703c895c348dd6b075915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1b6823080a36e51cc808c3830681953289500f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = \\frac{S_k}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647271e4a6b6fd0de6eb451e23e030e49ddf2893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{k+1} = S_k + a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295cb09b3f4e9bc62d01c7eef25a6084889bce08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{k+1} = \\frac{b_k \\cdot k + a_{k+1}}{k+1} = \\left(\\frac{k}{k+1}\\right) \\cdot b_k + \\frac{a_{k+1}}{k+1}\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c72db5be7b2854ffd5d03f88920fb872672af3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{k+1} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />, and by definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea3699554c894d8d044a4643987b30b228b95730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{k+1}}{k+1} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"77\" height=\"34\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de85f82298777eedf7546a4bd09712951e2b270a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} &lt; b_k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />. Also, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9e9d4cc5fd858d837b4334ffb04e2f62819500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> are integers, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294368c67c6a240e071c404d52eb34c0303bb062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} \\le b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />. As the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />'s form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Non-increasing&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Non-increasing (page does not exist)\">non-increasing</a> sequence of positive integers, they must eventually become constant. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82f3f9232cfe7ad32c5fc8e71113dcd693b54fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> for some sufficiently large value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d4c4cae28db9151cc38041e9026c7604d32492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = S_{k+1} - S_k = b_k(k + 1) - b_k(k) = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"334\" height=\"18\" />, so eventually the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> becomes constant.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bf6d7656718f44b05db794584495187f058493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91206ae50f0901e5d1090eee97b0414f46b88b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k\\leq k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a251e20b5a84eee2e7982cbbf343c01cad702c45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n\\leq n + 1 + 2 + \\cdots + n - 1 = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}.\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"38\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d021d719c660fa174ac5bdbedf7967f79bff0db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n = nk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we can keep adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to satisfy the conditions, provided that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c97c58c0a33cbe81e87888d21ab5e1d60fa2381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. This is true since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb71c971bb9224060726ba086f98b80ae592983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\leq\\frac{n + 1}{2}\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />, so the sequence must eventually become constant.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bdc4c41a6437428498703c895c348dd6b075915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1b6823080a36e51cc808c3830681953289500f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = \\frac{S_k}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />. By the problem hypothesis, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer valued sequence.\n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> There exists a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d786b6d7a1ebd2f5011a7b4581620ff447dedb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof:</i> Choose any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/267629a4bdf74f3287767a45b4ff64e1348552c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 3k - 2 &gt; 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967129a50841e3942fd090f7301c9efb4b8e0bf2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{k^2 + 3k - 2}{2} &amp;&gt; n \\\\ k^2 &amp;&gt; \\frac{k^2 - 3k + 2}{2} + n \\\\ k^2 &amp;&gt; (k-2) + (k-1) + \\cdots + 1 + n \\\\ k^2 &amp;&gt; a_{k-1} + a_{k-2} + \\cdots + a_2 + a_1 \\\\ k^2 &amp;&gt; S_k \\\\ k &amp;&gt; \\frac{S_k}{k} \\\\ k &amp;&gt; b_k, \\end{align*}\" width=\"357\" height=\"235\" />\nas desired.\n</p><p><b>End Lemma</b>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d786b6d7a1ebd2f5011a7b4581620ff447dedb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea7a111d351b838670b4cc5061601c77eea10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = m &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77358976ab0fd683d45db32b1b14d05bb11787c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = km$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />. To make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9e9d4cc5fd858d837b4334ffb04e2f62819500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647271e4a6b6fd0de6eb451e23e030e49ddf2893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{k+1} = S_k + a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b8afd8a3d042b0016f3d5ff0484783d7e5225e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$km + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239a6286344f110e42c45cf93c339f6566f6b7be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} \\equiv m \\pmod{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />, and, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d9c85e6fa1ff3c89c2da7f176504d4dce33c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_{k+1} &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a3dc2fc7349fc358127e4e6895f6fe638a35b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7ca0fee0ff8d774df4d96ca41ba86f6d9b452e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1} = \\frac{(k+1)m}{k+1} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"172\" height=\"40\" /> as well. Repeating the same process using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658a60632dd79ae8d8b6c93e1e0744b0f98304b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+2} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />, and an easy induction can prove that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a4fb6dcd85954476fbe651411cb1c2ef656b657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &gt; k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967f11f68eda475da17bd18c6948c78bd61a9d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_N = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> becomes a constant function for arbitrarily large values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c779d0ba2c47e7587d30a6d8c860c8d24603fa32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d3291c444b628695351aafa370a84cc19437fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s_k = a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_k.\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" />\nWe claim that for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34e049cc47a5f72e648f7b3b99d68e00f7c1d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_m = m(m - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. To this end, consider the sequence which computes the differences between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc028050428615cc28ee3c1f9a67eda8e9a726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39181bc6b6f88f2fb66a20745c4044d4321384ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, i.e., whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-th term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/163e5c79838dc55215b649196c9599ddc74234bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k - k(k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. Note that the first term of this sequence is positive (it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) and that its terms are strictly decreasing since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/6219226b4bdb048cf75b17aba102a371e052ae02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(s_k - k(k - 1)) - (s_{k+1} - (k + 1)k) = 2k - a_{k+1}\\geq 2k - k = k\\geq 1.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" />\nFurther, a negative term cannot immediately follow a positive term. Suppose otherwise, namely that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486e3b8ed2b05f4220f79f6d179b82bbc8886056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k &gt; k(k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/49881b7423cc62c2694e9133e1085dd7e3abfd17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{k+1} &lt; (k + 1)k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc028050428615cc28ee3c1f9a67eda8e9a726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc100eed327049453bbdcaa04c6edaa0eef51bb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, we can tighten the above inequalities to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401084fe9f4a2eb9f70dc7159321adb03da5f98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k\\geq k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833dd3d18e3888949f9d7a5f5e3cd02bd70da178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{k+1}\\leq (k + 1)(k - 1) = k^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"19\" />. But this would imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c4949feb02f8c704614eca47c97f374a453b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k &gt; s_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, a contradiction. We conclude that the sequence of differences must eventually include a term equal to zero.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34e049cc47a5f72e648f7b3b99d68e00f7c1d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_m = m(m - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. We claim that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd86c27879e257c571ce5e078d893235524f21a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m - 1 = a_{m+1} = a_{m+2} = a_{m+3} = a_{m+4} = \\cdots.\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"16\" />\nThis follows from the fact that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a82e7c7dbf7b035a66b5890ec80463b4c3e8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> is uniquely determined and choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c3772452e8cab579e18eb7b7fb8a402f28edb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m+i} = m - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6f5ccabae7a15544c550d5e72889aa4ca4ed93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" />, satisfies the range condition\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef295657ddaacad86d5727b3b140d42c44baacd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0\\leq a_{m+i} = m - 1\\leq m + i - 1,\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"17\" />\nand yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e7726b5454f4d4a5a4e1783c1f43bf496fcc84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s_{m+i} = s_m + i(m - 1) = m(m - 1) + i(m - 1) = (m + i)(m - 1).\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379f198b8825d847a983b3374011ad7802ae1b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k =\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"89\" height=\"56\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801bddc326fb1def4259d3724eaa4a121d0d542c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293484e302058afb36834db43bc6d6d0f91fb6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a_k &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1277d2696b534d587da6a27b7dccf3ca8dc3daa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k = S_k / k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c63cd4c6d6f2e1b1d8787aca407c1cbdd1cddde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>First, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec938f1b6c71d682d7280bb5fef91cfd2cc5f42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{k-1} = (k-1) \\cdot m_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c192bfcbc2607509034cddb71f9e9da6f345ea0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = S_{k-1} + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801bddc326fb1def4259d3724eaa4a121d0d542c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/36718e73ad226572e4b66053b3368575c0b5846c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\equiv m_{k-1} \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f8c3057b1e7e56c152431a367904b0e10a0dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k \\bmod k \\equiv \\bigl((k-1) \\cdot m_{k-1} + (m_{k-1} \\bmod k)\\bigr) \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"432\" height=\"24\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e3e1c1dc58ab917e4e349ee64f0d42268dc4cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-1) \\cdot m_{k-1} \\equiv -m_{k-1} \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f559f06358ad74a3a50180a8bd52b98620258d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-m_{k-1} + (m_{k-1} \\bmod k) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />, this holds.\n</p><p>Next, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d3b72d816226d813c2128e97fff5f01d95c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k = S_k / k = \\bigl((k-1) \\cdot m_{k-1} + a_k\\bigr) / k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"298\" height=\"24\" />. \nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e82032dbd77f829294f4ebe1ec53d3d5154477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{k-1} \\geq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44db28a2f5afb3c7a775a9e69f88c08515011ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{k-1} = qk + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448373459eeb31ff43255ae41e6a3281ac99f292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq r &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc698fa070cb2d526d4d1fc70f60a828c0c5af92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc9181657a8412888cb5f7bd640ce81cf7fe317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k = \\frac{(k-1) \\cdot m_{k-1} + r}{k} &lt; m_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"260\" height=\"40\" />,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3efee75259e0915441732d349588a0076b06bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_k &lt; m_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />. Moreover, so long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e82032dbd77f829294f4ebe1ec53d3d5154477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{k-1} \\geq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/208adf4a30ab30124fdb3c5c977d70ff04b678bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> is strictly decreasing while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is strictly increasing, until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8d53ca53cb3dbd06d061f449ae66e9371f05f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i} \\leq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />, in which case the sequence terminates as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b41506f227413342ddb689675645a06a000a98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{k-1} = m_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_6.28like_solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6(like_solution_2)\">Solution 6(like solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6(like solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, we may make an observation and say that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10cb51ac6525c7ae785a8232e33f815bf41b367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv p (mod k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cad86207facc595000ab9c62496b07a98a55cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{m=2}^{k} a_m \\equiv k-p (mod k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"180\" height=\"56\" /> must occur for the whole sum to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the following is apparent:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71dbf10570954a333d3d4632b50cb09fc68a910.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m=2}^{k} a_m =(q+1)k - p , k &lt; n\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"50\" />\nThen, we may make another observation that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fbf6b1b2bc81af471428fe2dc93cf475d6cd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, the sum also has to be divisible by n. We may then explore when n=k:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d034f645e7c00a18bef8323009b0bef86e5eaae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m=2}^{n} a_m \\equiv 0 (mod n), \\sum_{m=2}^{n} a_m = rn\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"47\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1839fe1aacba895e7f11a64656a1b844b6e9e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = \\sum_{m=2}^{n} a_m - \\sum_{m=2}^{n-1} a_m\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"50\" />\nThen,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f6421551836a4b4c299490ecd810c65064766e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = rn - \\sum_{m=2}^{n-1} a_m \\le n-1\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"50\" />\nAlso,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f592c048ca5bb1b406f63b750cb22d8edaf46f67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+s} = r, r \\le n\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddeeb641a373b1e7af8ced556090513f4878baae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. This is because:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf190066dd1aab2692647378651f6e4be2a02f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m=2}^{n} a_m + r = rn + r = r(n+1)\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"47\" />\nThis must be true since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/84166c6c4dd4b89fdda8099c9aa6d99b18111713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> will be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/504a6b6cb84114918789434311ba096bc77bff25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, we may then generalize this to all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800ad0b5ffa00d236710c352c65b8ae1b19bccd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(n+s), s \\in \\mathbb{Z}, s \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d238e6eade0de0b8f0a914c4cdf10e95b01d43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[rn + sr= r(n+s), \\frac{r(n+s)}{r} = n + s = \\frac{\\sum_{m=2}^{n+s} a_m}{r}\\]\" width=\"389\" height=\"42\" />\nThus, we may say that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f035420254f2a5b7094cd514f8937c52c998a54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,...a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"11\" /> must converge to some integer value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273bd71505ae1e25be49f77df7890476f83b9f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7c50bcfe62f0edb653edf6c8c8965f4d272ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7.28A_simpler_version_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7(A_simpler_version_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 7(A simpler version of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7(A simpler version of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d663378a98b4ba41e6eecb0a24ba37a562bac98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1 \\cdot x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a669d842794490df0ee4f4eef0e9ba2c7368f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2=2 \\cdot x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423fbe7fa583b8acd6d6ecddc04671bb410ea784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+a_3=3 \\cdot x_3, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Claim.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a483e1defd8c874301b3c451f9133dc1b41fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\geq x_2 \\geq x_3 \\geq ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Proof.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a728580655af114cc04d0a35efbd8461873cb14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2 \\cdot x_2 - 1 \\cdot x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b9864426f794d438cf95fe7651435e383790b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=3 \\cdot x_3 - 2 \\cdot x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc6c63a53a44e81e7abd70fa191de4d632cd4da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=4 \\cdot x_4 - 3 \\cdot x_3, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>F.T.S.O.C suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309ed75688c74f8173db06f66602094f3694cbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1} &lt; x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e1ab29602d2bd4412e1f05b9612a45ce661154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=n \\cdot x_n - (n-1) \\cdot x_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/46183ce7a2c978b9115e77b44412208d51723146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot x_n &gt; (n-1) \\cdot (x_{n-1}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/3940a8e33e5ec11e6c856d14f027c8cc9fba8f00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n \\geq x_{n-1}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This directly implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf43ff833a4ef34899255ceb658526623304065a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot x_n - (n-1) \\cdot x_{n-1} = a_n &gt; n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" />, a contradiction to the bound given on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> by the problem.\n</p><p>Hence, it is impossibe to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309ed75688c74f8173db06f66602094f3694cbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1} &lt; x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, implying  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3ecb9e81584cba846d12e9cbcf76abe0b16bd9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1} \\geq x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a483e1defd8c874301b3c451f9133dc1b41fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\geq x_2 \\geq x_3 \\geq ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, proving our claim.\n</p><p><br />\nAs the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> only consists of positive integers, it can't be ever decreasing, so that it must become eventually constant, \n</p><p>that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f3babbe6a8c0fa0016729563e080558618aa48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k=x_{k+1}=...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" /> from some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df9cf1d6f6e2474e61796d7425ac78ce112893b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Then, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8da116826e9029fc36d488ee11f8ad242bc5535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+...+a_k=k \\cdot x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f16f495cf4da295e7d395e91b3644daba77e86e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+...+a_k+a_{k+1}=(k+1) \\cdot x_{k+1}=(k+1) \\cdot x_k, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"416\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47cfb85a61253c9b006f2c6cb0455f7152752246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k=a_{k+1}=a_{k+2}=...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"14\" /> (by substracting the 1st equation from the 2nd, the 2nd from the 3rd, and so on), completing the proof to the problem.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=145842 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO\" title=\"2007 USAMO\">2007 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213947\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 869/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1634/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30006/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.539      1 -total\n 37.25%    6.533      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 32.72%    5.738      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 28.38%    4.978      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4888:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213947 and revision id 